DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("e^((x^3))");
$fun_1 = Formula("3*((x)^(1/3))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("{-6, -5, -4, 3, 10} - ((-infinity, infinity) - (({-6, -5, -4, 3, 10}))) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ((2, infinity)))");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("{-6, -5, -4, 3, 10} U (2, infinity)");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("{-5, -4, -3} - ((-infinity, infinity) - ((3, infinity))) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-5, -4, -3})");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("{-5, -4, -3} U (3, infinity)");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

- _For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._
- _For derivative problems, if the result is undefined, then *leave the blank empty*._

What is the value of [`19+12-19+16/18`]? [_____]{answer=>Formula('12.8888888889'),width=>1}
---

What is the value of [`14+4-17+0/11`]? [_____]{Real(1.)}
---

What is the value of [`6+1-11`]? [_____]{Formula('-4')}
---

What is the value of [`15+0-1+8*15`]? [_____]{134}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-5, -4, -3\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x > 2\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cap (B) \cap A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`A \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-6, -5, -4, 3, 10\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x \leq 11\}`]
- [`C = \{x | x > 1\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cap ((A)) \cap (C) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`A \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 4, 9, 1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -9, -5, -8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -6, 3, -1 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-6, 3, -1>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-9, -5, -8>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-9, -5, -8>") . Compute("<-6, 3, -1>")}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-9, -5, -8>") x Compute("<-6, 3, -1>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-9, -5, -8>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{w} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-6, 3, -1>") . Compute("<4, 9, 1>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -5, 10, -9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -7, 10, -5 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 0, 2, -5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-7, 10, -5>") x Compute("<-5, 10, -9>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-7, 10, -5>"))}
- [` \vec{w} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<0, 2, -5>") . Compute("<-7, 10, -5>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-5, 10, -9>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(3) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>3)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(6) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>6)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
